		{"id":"3ed1296d947699bf","type":"text","text":"# StemLoft\n\nDesktop app for playing back musical _stems_, focused on **creating loop repeats of sections using time markers**.\n\n## About\n\nStemLoft is a practice tool for **beginner musicians**. Starting from the stems of a song (isolated tracks for each instrument), the user marks a section on the timeline and the app repeats it continuously — letting them practice their part by playing along with, or in place of, an instrument from the original recording.\n\nThe user also controls the mixer for each stem (volume, mute, and solo), for example muting the instrument they're learning and playing over the rest of the track.\n\n## Main feature\n\n**Loop repeats via time markers.** Set a start and end marker on a section of the song and repeat it as many times as needed, at the recording's original tempo, with the other instruments playing normally.","x":-586,"y":-1080,"width":869,"height":520},
		{"id":"94ab3840c4ebd3e1","type":"text","text":"\n## Metadata\n\nPersisted as its own text file (no longer embedded in the project's .json): `Score Metadata Manager` does the parsing, `Project Persistence` only holds the reference to the file.\n\n### Format: extended ChordPro\n\nOpen standard (https://www.chordpro.org/), `.cho` extension. Already solves for free:\n\n| Need | Native ChordPro feature |\n|---|---|\n| Chord + lyrics together, as simply as possible | `[G]Amazing [C]grace` |\n| Exact chord fingering | `{define: G base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 3}` |\n| Instrumental section / free-form tablature | `{start_of_tab}` ... `{end_of_tab}` |\n| Song metadata | `{title}`, `{key}`, `{tempo}`, `{time}`, `{capo}` |\n\nTwo custom extensions:\n\n- `{tuning: E A D G B E}` - tuning, lowest string->highest (same order `frets` already uses in `{define}`).\n- `{t: mm:ss.cc}` - absolute time anchor (in the style of .lrc), at the start of a line. Its own directive instead of `[00:12.34]`-style brackets, because brackets are already ChordPro's chord syntax.\n\nUnknown directives are ignored by any standard ChordPro reader — the file stays useful outside of StemLoft.\n\n\nExact format of `{t:}`: `minute \":\" second \".\" hundredth` — minute 1+ digits with no leading zero, second always 2 digits (00-59), hundredth always 2 digits (00-99). \"0:00.00\" valid; \"1:5.3\" not valid.\n\nDialect rule: at most one chord per line (plain ChordPro allows several, but {t:} only anchors the start of the line — a second chord on the same line would have no timestamp of its own). Phrases with a chord change mid-line become two lines.\n\nGuitar technique notation inside `{start_of_tab}`, in the format `<fret><technique><fret>...`:\n\n| Symbol | Technique | Example | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| h | Hammer-on | 5h7 | Play fret 5 and sound fret 7 on the same string, without picking again |\n| p | Pull-off | 7p5 | Play fret 7 and release to sound fret 5, without picking again |\n| b | Bend | 7b9 | Bend the string at fret 7 until it sounds like fret 9 |\n| r | Release | 7b9r7 | A bend followed by releasing back to fret 7 |\n| / | Slide up | 5/7 | Slide from fret 5 up to fret 7 |\n| \\\\ | Slide down | 7\\5 | Slide from fret 7 down to fret 5 |\n| ~ | Vibrato | 8~ | Vibrate the note at fret 8 |\n\n\n\n#### Resolving startSec/endSec and grid origin\n\n- `endSec` of a chord = `{t:}` of the next event that changes what's sounding (next [chord] or next {start_of_tab}) — a lyric line with no bracket does NOT end the current chord, it only advances the text.\n- Last chord in the file: `endSec` = duration of the longest stem (or a final line with {t:} + [chord] repeated, just to close the window).\n- Grid origin (bar 1, beat 1) = first `{t:}` in the file, not necessarily second 0 of the audio.\n- Time inside a {start_of_tab}: a single {t:} anchor at the start; each note's position is proportional to the character's column on the line — noteSec = startSec + (column/totalColumns) x (endSec - startSec).\n\n#### Grammar\n\n```\nitem        := note (\"-\" note)* | \"-\"        ; \"-\" alone = rest\nnote        := fret (op fret | \"~\")* \".\" string\nop          := \"h\" | \"p\" | \"b\" | \"r\" | \"/\" | \"\\\"\nfret        := digit digit?                  ; 0-24, no leading zero\nstring      := \"1\" | \"2\" | \"3\" | \"4\" | \"5\" | \"6\"\ndigit       := \"0\"..\"9\"\n```\n\n`~` is the only operator with no target fret. Validation rules: `r` is only valid after a `b` in the same note; two notes in the same item can't point to the same string; fret 0-24; string 1-6.\n\n### Full example — chords + lyrics\n\n```\n{title: Study in G Major}\n{artist: StemLoft - example}\n{key: G}\n{time: 4/4}\n{tempo: 80}\n{tuning: E A D G B E}\n\n{define: G base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 3}\n{define: C base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 0}\n{define: D base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 2}\n\n{t: 0:00.00}\n[G]First time I pick up the guitar\n{t: 0:03.00}\n[C]My fingers still hurt, but I'll keep going\n{t: 0:06.00}\n[D]Every chord is a step I climb\n{t: 0:09.00}\n[G]One day I'll play this song without thinking\n```\n\n### Example with techniques — instrumental section\n\n```\n{title: Phrase with Techniques}\n{key: Am}\n{time: 4/4}\n{tempo: 100}\n{tuning: E A D G B E}\n\n{c: Instrumental interlude - A minor pentatonic}\n{t: 0:00.00}\n{start_of_tab}\nE|----------------------------------------------------------------|\nB|-5h8-----8p5---------------------------------------------8~-----|\nG|-----------------7-----------------------7b9-----7b9r7----------|\nD|-------------------------5/7-----7\\5----------------------------|\nA|----------------------------------------------------------------|\nE|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n{end_of_tab}\n```\n\n### How this resolves points 1-4 of the analysis\n\n1. No authoring component -> resolved for v1, not dropped as a feature: v1 is read-only (the app doesn't write the .cho, the user edits it in an external editor). Editing chords in the UI itself (the app rewriting the .cho) is a real feature planned for after v1 - see TODO.md and architecture.md.\n2. Rigid beat-indexed grid -> resolved: no more array indexed by beat; chords sit loosely next to the syllable, tablature is free-form text inside `{start_of_tab}`.\n3. Unvalidated redundancy (sizeInBeats/beats/tabs.length) -> resolved: none of those fields exist anymore; duration comes from the actual audio or from the last `{t:}`.\n4. Two time domains with no conversion -> resolved: `{t: mm:ss.cc}` uses seconds, the same domain `Loop & Marker Manager` already uses.\n","x":-1680,"y":-1100,"width":943,"height":3400},
